WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.053
Welcome to Module 3: Design Qualification,
or DQ.

2
00:00:04.173 --> 00:00:10.040
Our fictional vessel V-201 prepares an
aqueous oral solution before filling.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.272
It is not an aseptic process.

4
00:00:12.392 --> 00:00:16.211
The diagram connects intended purpose to a
proposed design

5
00:00:16.331 --> 00:00:18.379
and then to a reasoned decision.

6
00:00:18.499 --> 00:00:21.848
We ask whether the design can support the
intended use.

7
00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.464
A purchase order or attractive equipment

8
00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:27.379
drawing cannot answer that question by
itself.

9
00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:30.665
DQ evaluates the proposed design.

10
00:00:30.785 --> 00:00:34.455
Installation qualification examines what
was installed.

11
00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:38.031
Operational qualification challenges
operation,

12
00:00:38.151 --> 00:00:40.540
and performance qualification addresses

13
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.329
performance for the intended use under
defined conditions.

14
00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:47.884
These questions are connected but not
interchangeable.

15
00:00:48.004 --> 00:00:50.095
A successful design review does

16
00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:55.036
not demonstrate that the installed vessel
mixes a real batch uniformly.

17
00:00:55.156 --> 00:00:58.207
Later modules examine those later stages.

18
00:00:58.327 --> 00:01:01.856
Keep the evidence and the decision
appropriate to the stage.

19
00:01:02.476 --> 00:01:06.060
Look at three design concerns: the product
contact path,

20
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.886
the measurement chain and access for
cleaning.

21
00:01:09.006 --> 00:01:13.187
A vessel can have a suitable steel body
yet an unsuitable gasket.

22
00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:15.307
A temperature display can work

23
00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:18.074
while representing the wrong sensor
location.

24
00:01:18.194 --> 00:01:21.117
A shiny exterior can conceal a trapped
pocket.

25
00:01:21.237 --> 00:01:25.098
For each concern, ask which design feature
addresses the need,

26
00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:29.122
what evidence supports that claim and what
must later be verified.

27
00:01:29.742 --> 00:01:33.582
In this course, every equipment
identifier, specification

28
00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:36.668
and evidence reference is a teaching
invention.

29
00:01:36.788 --> 00:01:39.284
No site equipment has been qualified.

30
00:01:39.404 --> 00:01:42.668
At the end of a DQ review, state the
design scope,

31
00:01:42.788 --> 00:01:45.860
the evidence examined and the open
conditions.

32
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.392
Do not write ready for routine production

33
00:01:48.512 --> 00:01:51.100
when only design evidence has been
assessed.

34
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.207
Your first activity is to distinguish a
design

35
00:01:54.327 --> 00:01:58.103
conclusion from an installation finding
and a performance claim.
